review:
Since this game is universally acclaimed, I will point three things that annoyed me:

There is a lack of resources even in standard mode. That combined with RNG drops and inconvenient autosaves can cause very hard situations;

There is no minimap;

And there is too many puzzles.

*Mr. X appears in an unexpected random place;
Me: 
-Ah ♥♥♥♥, here we go again...

As good a remake of one of the best survival horror games of all time as you could ask for. I've completed leon and claire's first playthrough's and it was for the most part a really enjoyable, tense experience. The tyrant following you around the police station can get pretty frustrating if you're caught out by him but i cant really fault much else in the game. 

if you're a fan of resident evil you probably already own this. if you don't, buy it :) 

5/5

This is the best Remake ever made.

[u]Pros[/u]
+ Nothing was really cut from the original game, lots of things were added or improved;
+ The engine is amazing with a really good gameplay;
+ Amazing graphics;
+ The game offers you a good challenge, getting an S+ Rank on Hardcore is really difficult;
+ The Ghost Survivor and other extra modes were a nice addition to the game;
+ Really good replayabillity;
+ Tons of mods available on the internet.

[u]Cons[/u]
- In the original game, Leon and Claire scenarios were the same but different, in the Remake they are different but the same. Capcom could have made them all different and canon, but missed the opportunity. They're all great, nevertheless;
- The redesign of Leon's face is very different from what we were used to, he looks like a soy boy now;
- All DLCs are paid mods cash grab garbage. They might be useful if you want mods, as most modders use those slots to add custom models.

